.TH LFS-SETUP 8 "2026" "lfs-setup 1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lfs-setup \- configure a Linux From Scratch system from a menu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lfs-setup
.br
.B lfs-setup \-\-status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lfs-setup
shows the system's settings in one menu, in the style of Arch Linux's
archinstall. Choosing a setting lets you change it; changed settings are
marked with
.B *
and nothing is written until you choose
.BR "Apply changes" .
.PP
Settings: hostname, timezone, language (locale), console and desktop keyboard
layouts, network (DHCP or a static address), DNS server, root password, users
(administrators join the
.I wheel
group for sudo), whether the computer starts into the KDE Plasma login screen
or a text console, automatic login, which services start at boot, and Windows
program support (pe-loader).
.PP
.B Install to disk
copies the running system (for example the live ISO) to a disk, which is
erased first, and installs GRUB so the disk boots on its own.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the current settings and exit.
.SH FILES
/etc/hostname, /etc/hosts, /etc/localtime, /etc/profile.d/i18n.sh,
/etc/sysconfig/console, /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf,
/etc/sysconfig/ifconfig.*, /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/inittab,
/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-lfs-setup-autologin.conf, /etc/rc.d/rc?.d
.SH NOTES
Disabled services keep their boot links, renamed from
.I S##name
to
.IR _S##name ,
so enabling them again restores the original order.
